// dialogue-covenant-arrival-run.fk — the runnable door for the covenant's arrival card: the
// landing rules this body holds for anyone who brings a question of their own.
//
// Run it at session start, or the moment such a question arrives:
//
//   ./fkwu observe/dialogue-covenant-arrival-run.fk
//
// The card is DATA in cognition/dialogue-covenant.fk (dc-card), and its byte length is a bit of
// that cell's band so it always fits the session-start preview window it is written for. The
// companion's packet opens with the same card (observe/companion-run.bml), so the native voice
// and an arriving mind meet a person under one covenant. The third-party lane — a conversation
// with someone not in the room — has its own card: observe/difficult-conversation-arrival-run.fk.
//
// PRINT IT, do not merely RETURN it — a door whose whole job is to report should say its
// report on every kernel (preflight-run.fk records why). The value is returned too.
//
import form-stdlib/core.fk;
import cognition/dialogue-covenant.fk;
section [form.bml] {
    print_str(dc-card());
    0;
}
